Sval: mozprocess reads a process's exit code without racing its reader

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 1933337 (mozilla-central 678211a7551d,
1bf2f8e2dd37 and 093301928869, Firefox 161), with the one-line change of
Bug 1916979 (mozilla-central e79b49bd6181, Firefox 160) the first of them
builds on, unchanged. ESR 153 carries none of them.
ProcessReader treats a deadline already passed as a timeout (Bug 1916979).
On Windows the exit code is read under the cleanup lock, so it never reads a
handle _cleanup is closing on another thread; Process.returncode is set in
one place only; and poll() no longer returns the None a timed-out wait()
stored once the reader thread has finished, which reported a process that
had exited as still running. Its test is mozprocess's test_poll.py.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 161.

